    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a calculated offensive approach, headlined by **Junior Caminero** (70.80) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (64.80). **Junior Caminero** is our strongest play; despite a slight park penalty, his elite SP skill adjustment against Sandy Alcantara suggests high-leverage production, bolstered by a prime #2 hole placement. Meanwhile, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is a mandatory start due to his disruptive speed profile and a strong 14% platoon edge against Davis Martin. While **Luke Raley** (62.62) ranks highly due to a favorable matchup against Walker Buehler, keep a close watch on **Trea Turner** (60.34) and **Kyle Schwarber** (57.29); both face a 32% rain risk in their clash with Bubba Chandler, which could dampen their output or lead to early exits.\n\nOur roster construction leans heavily into dynamic platoon advantages and volume to overcome tough individual matchups like **Yordan Alvarez** facing Jacob deGrom. Even with deGrom\u2019s pedigree, **Yordan Alvarez** remains a core start because his elite xwOBA floor offsets the SP difficulty. The tightest call on the bench involved **Hyeseong Kim** (49.35), who nearly cracked the lineup over **Christian Yelich** (48.83). While **Hyeseong Kim** benefited from a projected wind boost and a favorable platoon spot, the optimizer ultimately favored the veteran experience and lineup security of **Christian Yelich**. We continue to monitor the status of **Lars Nootbaar**, **Josh Smith**, **Luis Pena**, and **Pedro Ramirez**, while noting that **Zac Veen** and **Colt Keith** remain sidelined in the minors or on the bench, offering no immediate utility for today\u2019s 5x5 categories.",
